Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: match WBE1.3 QCN6432 host BDF capability

The original Acer QCN6432 WBE1.3 CNSS host-capability request does not
advertise BDF-support, although it passes a fixed BDF physical address
inside the HOST_DDR reservation later in the QMI memory response.

Avoid advertising a distinct host BDF service for this UserPD while
preserving the existing capability for other ath12k hardware. This is
a targeted firmware-contract experiment pending hardware validation.

---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2274,8 +2274,14 @@
 	req.num_clients = 1;
 	req.mem_cfg_mode = ab->qmi.target_mem_mode;
 	req.mem_cfg_mode_valid = 1;
-	req.bdf_support_valid = 1;
-	req.bdf_support = 1;
+	/* WBE 1.3 QCN6432 uses the vendor CNSS fixed-BDF contract:
+	 * the BDF resides inside HOST_DDR and is not separately offered
+	 * through the host BDF-support capability.
+	 */
+	if (ab->hw_rev != ATH12K_HW_QCN6432_HW10) {
+		req.bdf_support_valid = 1;
+		req.bdf_support = 1;
+	}
 
 	if (ab->hw_params->fw.m3_loader == ath12k_m3_fw_loader_driver) {
 		req.m3_support_valid = 1;
